# Ignore every subfolder's contents, keep this file and the README tracked.
#
# This is the Task 0.4 rule, and it is deliberately a blanket one rather than a
# list of dataset names. The root .gitignore also names specific folders
# (datasets/drive/, datasets/idrid/ ...), but those entries are lowercase and
# the actual download unzips as `DRIVE/`. On Windows that still matches, because
# the filesystem is case-insensitive; on Linux or macOS it does NOT, and a
# teammate would commit twenty real patient fundus photographs without git
# saying a word.
#
# A pattern that only works on some of the team's machines is worse than none,
# because it appears to work right up until it doesn't. Match everything here
# and let the exceptions be explicit.
*/

# ...except the two files that document what should be here.
!README.md
!.gitignore

# Original archives, whatever they are named.
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.7z
